2.2: 7
Prove that if a smooth $f : RR^n -> RR^n$ is non-singular at $x_0$ then the induced map $H_n(RR^n, RR^n - x_0) -> H_n(RR^n, RR^n - f(x_0))$ is $"id"$ or $- "id"$ according
to whether $D f(x_0)$ is orientation preserving or
reversing.

